WEBVTT

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:06.040
If I could have understood
human emotions of that sort,

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.510
would I have been able
to better interact with Remy?

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.550
You're basically taking the place
of Remy's parents, aren't you?

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.430
Xi! That's crazy!

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.020
Xi is going to protect me...

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.680
Remy! I'll save you now!

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:33.030
Goodbye, Remy. May you find happiness...

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.370
I will protect you.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.670
You have opened Pandora's Box
with your own hands.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.610
An Energy Cube?

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.530
<i>Everyone, can you hear me?
Do you copy?</i>

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:16.490
Kumi?

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:18.200
<i>This is an emergency.</i>

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.540
<i>We will now commence
the forced return sequence.</i>

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.600
Where am I?

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.030
The forced return packs a punch, doesn't it?

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:00.200
Do you understand what's taking place?

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.450
Dr. Odhner?

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.830
Go ahead and restrain them.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:17.470
Let me out—

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.510
Stop that. It's dangerous.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.600
I'm sorry for being so rough with you.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:32.860
Dr. Odhner...

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:36.740
But this was also necessary,

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:42.580
so that we humans
can evolve to the next stage.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.790
What do you mean?

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.330
I'll explain that.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.790
You're...

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:56.720
Let me introduce you.
This is my other self from the Frontier world...

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.470
Doctor Odhner.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:37.400
You were the catalyst, 
Kazasumi from this world.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:42.070
Sudden Turn: The Price of Arrogance

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.030
I was?

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.650
The fact that you came to Frontier,

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:46.160
and that the Tohru Kazasumi 
from my world came here.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:50.870
As a result, we were able to learn
each other's coordinates.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.670
Each other's...

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:59.460
Once we know the coordinates,
it's not difficult to contact each other.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:05.930
After finding out about each other's worlds,
we tried to devise a way to counter the Timekeepers.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:11.470
But Kazasumi, the data you brought back
changed the situation.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.560
The data I brought back?

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:15.690
That's right.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.730
The Energy Cube that you used
to defeat the Dead End

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:26.490
and the data gained from its analysis will
further human technology by a hundred years.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:29.530
Actually, "evolve" may be a better word.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:35.790
But there's a serious 
obstacle to overcome first.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:41.050
We decided to cooperate with each other
in order to remove that obstacle.

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:43.880
An obstacle... what is it?

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:45.550
All of you.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:48.600
Those capable of time transfer.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:57.100
That's right. We decided to join forces
to stop you from running rampant.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:05:59.690
Roger.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:00.610
What's up?

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.980
They're telling us to return immediately.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:07.950
They're saying that due to the spacetime storm earlier,
the spacetime is very unstable now

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:11.490
and that's why neither Kumi nor the doctor
are available on comm right now.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:14.250
It affected the chain of command?

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.460
That's unexpected...

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:22.250
On top of that, if we miss the window in six minutes,
we might be stuck in the 21st century.

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:28.760
That huge Energy Cube popped up,
but we don't even have the time to retrieve it...

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:33.060
The doctor is saying that
they'll think of something for that later.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.180
What do you think?

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:36.980
I don't know.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:40.940
Something about Tohru going back before us
doesn't sit right with me, either.

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:45.150
But if it's a trap,
we storm in and rip it to shreds.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.660
In either case, we can't take
 action from the 21st century.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.370
Roger. Then, let's head back.

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:58.040
Running rampant? What do you mean?

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:05.550
It seems you don't understand
how dangerous your actions have been.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:06.550
Dangerous?

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:08.840
We're talking about Kyohma.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:12.350
His decisions are spur-of-the-moment,

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:16.270
and it's only due to luck that 
they've gone as well as they have.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:21.020
For instance, in the previous 
operation in Asakusa

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:24.980
if you'd been hit by a stray bullet,
what would've happened?

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:31.320
No matter how much trust we have in you,
in that situation we should prepare backup personnel.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:34.120
However, he didn't do that.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:40.250
There's no way that will work forever.
It's like walking on a tightrope.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:44.500
Someone has to do something 
before everything is ruined.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:47.880
And by someone, you mean the two of you?

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.510
How perceptive.

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:55.140
It seems you're more talented
than the Tohru Kazasumi from my world.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:56.920
What a ridiculous idea!

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:57.890
Kazasumi!

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:02.440
Because you're Kyohma's friend,
I understand that you'd be upset.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:06.940
We were rather forceful in this.
For that, I apologize.

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:09.320
I want you to understand.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:13.570
We've spent a long time
working hard behind the scenes

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:16.990
in order to deal with the
problems Kyohma's causing,

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.080
but we're about to face annihilation.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:26.710
The very idea of having just a small number of
time travelers fight was insane to begin with.

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:29.960
But Kyohma is doing everything he can.
That's true of everyone.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:34.720
I thought we needed everyone's 
strength to fight the Timekeepers!

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:41.850
That was indeed true until a short while ago.
That's why we were obeying him.

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.230
However, now everything is different.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:45.980
What's different?

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.530
What are you talking about?

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:51.950
It's all thanks to the data
you brought back with you.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:56.740
With it, we can make
as many Energy Cubes as we want!

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:03.580
If we can recreate that technology,
there's no need to fear the Timekeepers.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:08.210
Wait! That was only possible
because we had that girl's powers.

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:11.590
Without those powers, we'd end up
creating a Dead End instead!

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:16.470
Rest assured, we're fully 
aware of your report.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:23.060
As long as we, the two greatest minds in this world,
are here, something like that is child's play.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:27.980
Humanity will, in due time, be free from
the menace known as the Timekeepers.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:30.690
All thanks to us.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:37.450
From Kumi? What's this?

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:47.580
It looks like I won't be bored.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.210
It's me.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:55.930
I see. Thanks for everything.

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:59.600
Keep them in confinement.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.720
We've captured Kyohma.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:08.940
What are you going to do with Kyohma?

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.880
We're not going to do anything.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.030
As long as he doesn't interrupt
 my plan, he'll be fine.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:19.030
That is, if you're willing 
to cooperate with me.

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:21.330
So you mean he's a hostage?

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.620
No, that's not what I mean.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:29.750
If you're with us, there's no need
to do anything to Kyohma, that's all.

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:30.500
Me?

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:36.590
No matter how brilliant we are,
it will take time for us to create a new weapon.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:42.140
However, with your help, we should
be able to greatly shorten that time.

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:47.100
With the information from the future
that you witnessed,

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.650
we should be able to create
a far superior technology.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.530
You're an intelligent boy.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:59.160
You're aware of which choice
is the most beneficial, yes?

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:03.540
<i>Don't do it, Kazasumi!</i>

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:04.480
What?

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:05.160
What happened?

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:07.580
<i>I'm releasing the energy barrier
in the restraining room.</i>

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:08.500
Kumi!

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:09.790
<i>Please escape!</i>

00:11:12.710 --> 00:11:13.630
Wait!

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:19.880
Good God. Kumi of all people...

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:23.810
The security troops are coming.
I want you to go back for now.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:26.430
I'll make things work here.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:30.690
Understood. Good luck, Dr. Odhner.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:34.230
Yes, same for you, Doctor Odhner.

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:41.280
Kumi... So they've gotten to you too?

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:43.370
What a shame.

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:50.870
<i>Notice to all level 3 and level 4 personnel.
Capture the fugitive Tohru Kazasumi.</i>

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:55.300
<i>If necessary, you're authorized to open fire.
Don't let him out of Block C!</i>

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:05.810
This is Sidune's?

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:08.060
Well, it's not to my taste, but...

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:10.100
It's a protective charm.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:41.300
Kazasumi!

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:51.850
Then everyone else is all right?

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:54.940
Yes. I've already contacted a few of them.

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:56.110
I'm glad.

00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:00.360
I'm sorry, Kazasumi,
that all of this happened...

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:03.410
Why would Dr. Odhner do this?

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:11.870
He's never been satisfied
with Kyohma being in charge.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:20.590
He used to rant that letting the time-travelers
keep a monopoly on the Energy Cubes was dangerous.

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:25.430
That's why, even now, he's actually 
doing what he thinks is right...

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:32.730
No, that's not quite it.

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:37.360
He's a child. He wants to
be acknowledged by someone.

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:41.780
In the end, his motive
is to leave his mark as a scientist.

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:47.700
So that's why he did something like that.
Human evolution?

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:50.870
That's exactly what creates the Dead End.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:55.580
But now, I'm sure Dr. Odhner
won't listen to what anyone else says.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.380
Even me. If he finds me, I'm sure...

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:05.340
Why is recognition so important to men?
It's so stupid.

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:08.890
Even if something was started 
with good intentions,

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:12.390
if you go down the wrong path,
it ends up as something terrible.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:15.270
Just like the Dead End.

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:20.230
Let's stop the doctor.
First, we have to get everyone together.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:28.620
Okay, I'm trusting you
with Remy, Kyohma, and the others.

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:30.030
Leave it to me.

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:34.370
You please be careful as well.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:35.370
Right.

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:38.960
<i>Lyudmila here.</i>

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:42.750
Lyudmila! I'm glad you're all right!

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:44.960
<i>I'll take over from here.</i>

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:46.170
I'll leave it to you.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:48.130
But still...

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:51.390
Is it okay to be this blatant?

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:56.140
<i>I've already hacked the security cameras
so that you don't show up on them.</i>

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:57.770
<i>What's left...</i>

00:14:57.770 --> 00:15:02.770
...is for me not to get spotted
by the patrolling soldiers, right?

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:06.780
<i>Yes. Let's do our best
in order to finish this battle.</i>

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:09.490
<i>I'll show you the route. Please proceed.</i>

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:10.570
Roger.

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:17.040
You still haven't found Kazasumi?

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:20.460
<i>Not yet. He hasn't shown up
on any of the security cameras.</i>

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:24.250
<i>Right now, we're continuing our search,
mainly in the cameras' blind spots.</i>

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:27.130
Understood. Keep at it, please.

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:33.890
How are the time-travelers 
doing in confinement?

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:36.180
<i>Sir, not much movement here.</i>

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:40.150
<i>A soldier is with the wounded Kyoka Katagiri
under the guise of being a bodyguard.</i>

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:41.520
What about Lyudmila?

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:45.190
<i>The medical machine is continuing treatment,
but she's still unconscious.</i>

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:48.280
Understood. Keep watch.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:49.200
<i>Roger.</i>

00:15:57.370 --> 00:16:02.000
Since Kumi guided them,
I didn't think this would be a cakewalk, but...

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:10.970
Not only have I lost Kazasumi,
but I've lost track of Remy's whereabouts as well...

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:14.800
Can it be that he's already escaped
from the laboratory?

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:21.310
No... everything else aside,
I don't think Kazasumi would forsake his friends.

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:25.900
Recorded footage, Lyudmila's room.
One hour ago.

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:29.150
Overlap the two images.

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:37.160
Enlarge to D-3.

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:47.170
Her IV levels haven't changed!

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:48.550
Damn it!

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:50.090
Calling all personnel!

00:16:51.130 --> 00:16:54.720
<i>Those eligible for time-space transfer
have hacked into the security camera network!</i>

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:59.100
Purge the system and
physically capture them, dead or alive!

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.360
Damn it...

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:08.190
Why has it come to this?!

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:15.780
At the very end... are you going
to make me dirty my own hands?

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:29.500
<i>Dr. Odhner has noticed my hacking.</i>

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:32.010
<i>I apologize.</i>

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.590
<i>It has become difficult for me
to support you any further.</i>

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:36.800
<i>I'll be making my exit now as well.</i>

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:40.060
Understood. I'll get by somehow on this end.

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:44.980
<i>Kyoka's location hasn't changed.
Are you okay with the route?</i>

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:48.060
Yes. I've memorized the entire map.

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:52.690
<i>After you rescue Kyoka,
please head to the exit point.</i>

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:54.740
<i>Best of luck.</i>

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.630
I've fulfilled the mission objective.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:12.630
Now, I leave everything up to you, Tohru...

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:24.730
It's time to atone for 
all the lives I've taken.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:34.570
Weapons?

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:35.700
Use this.

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:38.620
What about Jonathan and Matsurika?

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:40.450
The kids went on ahead.

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:45.040
Then we need to be a bit flashy
so we get all eyes on us!

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:53.510
So here's where you've been 
hiding them. Naughty child.

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:09.230
Now, I have to take enough
to give to everyone else.

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:11.360
Okay.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:30.040
<i>As I get closer to Kyoka's room,
the number of soldiers is increasing.</i>

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:33.800
<i>I'm sure it's on Dr. Odhner's orders...
but what should I do?</i>

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:36.760
Kyoka!

00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:59.700
Kyoka, are you all right?

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:01.740
Tohru!

00:20:05.540 --> 00:20:07.750
I got a message from Kumi.

00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:11.580
She told me to escape
and meet up with you, Tohru!

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:14.250
I see. I'm glad.

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:15.920
I'm sorry I'm late—

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:19.510
No. I'm glad you came for me.

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:25.970
There's all sorts of things I want to tell you,
but that discussion will have to wait.

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:30.480
Yup. For now, let's get out of here.

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:33.810
It's all right to go slow.
Let's move a little bit at a time.

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:35.360
I'm fine.

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:38.440
I'm the best girl in my gym class!

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:01.260
I guessed that would be the result.

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:07.810
Humanity cannot give up the Energy Cubes.

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:11.770
Even if they know that
they're their path to the Dead End...

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:16.520
Without Energy Cubes,
they can't win their battle.

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:20.610
That's why they use them,
because they don't want to lose.

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:28.660
No matter how much they run,
they cannot escape.

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:34.830
Because Dead End is the 
very ideal of humanity.

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:38.710
To deny that is the same as denying humanity.

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:46.260
All we need to do is wait...

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:51.220
...for all of you to reach the Dead End.

00:23:25.530 --> 00:23:27.070
I want to experience romance for once.

00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:29.110
Start a romance too fast
and you'll break up immediately!

00:23:29.110 --> 00:23:30.530
It's the aesthetics of extinction!

00:23:30.530 --> 00:23:31.830
I don't have a partner.

00:23:31.830 --> 00:23:34.200
You can just find one
somewhere around here.

00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:35.230
"Somewhere around here..."

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:37.210
Wh-Why are you looking my way?

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:38.350
Next episode: "Counterattack."

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:39.920
<b><i>COUNTERATTACK </i></b>THE DESTINATION OF EMOTIONS

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:39.920
"The Destination of Emotions."
